  "id": "Compound::DB06725 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Lornoxicam is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c9 through a series of binding interactions that ultimately converge on the enzyme. The evidence suggests that Lornoxicam binds to Ptgs1, which is then bound by various compounds, including Mefenamic Acid and Sulfamethoxazole, all of which in turn bind to Cyp2c9. This indicates a potential pathway where Lornoxicam may influence Cyp2c9 through the modulation of its binding partners. The lowest common ancestors of these interactions—Hydroxides and Organonitrogen Heterocyclic Compounds—highlight a shared functional role in the metabolic pathway. While the exact mechanism by which Lornoxicam affects Cyp2c9 remains unclear, the evidence points to a complex network of interactions that may involve the enzyme's regulation through the binding of its substrates and inhibitors. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering the broader context of drug-target interactions in understanding the pharmacological effects of Lornoxicam.",
